WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.440
There are 4 types of analytics:
• Descriptive analytics&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.760
• Diagnostic analytics
• Predictive analytics&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.080
• Prescriptive analytics

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.320
The more complex an analysis&nbsp;
is, the more value it brings.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.520
Descriptive analytics&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.800
Descriptive analytics answers the question&nbsp;
of what happened. For instance, a healthcare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.200
provider will learn how many patients were&nbsp;
hospitalized last month; a retailer - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.480
average weekly sales volume; a manufacturer – a&nbsp;
rate of the products returned for a past month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.640
etc. Descriptive analytics juggles raw data&nbsp;
from multiple data sources to give valuable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.560
insights into the past. However, these findings&nbsp;
simply signal that something is wrong or right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.560
without explaining why. For this reason, highly&nbsp;
data-driven companies do not content themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.600
with descriptive analytics only, and prefer&nbsp;
combining it with other types of data analytics.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.000
Diagnostic analytics
At this stage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.800
historical data can be measured against other data&nbsp;
to answer the question of why something happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.920
Thanks to diagnostic analytics,&nbsp;
there is a possibility to drill down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:28.240
to find out dependencies and to identify&nbsp;
patterns. Companies go for diagnostic analytics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.960
as it gives in-depth insights into&nbsp;
a particular problem. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.320
in the healthcare industry, analysis of customer&nbsp;
segmentation coupled with several filters applied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.680
such as diagnoses and prescribed medications,&nbsp;
allowed measuring the risk of hospitalization.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.800
Predictive analytics&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.440
Predictive analytics tells&nbsp;
what is likely to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.760
It uses the findings of descriptive and diagnostic&nbsp;
analytics to detect tendencies, clusters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.720
and exceptions, and to predict future trends,&nbsp;
which makes it a valuable tool for forecasting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.480
Despite numerous advantages that predictive&nbsp;
analytics brings, it is essential to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.520
that forecasting is just an estimate, the accuracy&nbsp;
of which highly depends on data quality and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.640
stability of the situation, so it requires a&nbsp;
careful treatment and continuous optimization.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.320
Thanks to predictive analytics and the proactive&nbsp;
approach it enables, a telecom company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.040
for instance, can identify the subscribers&nbsp;
who are most likely to reduce their spend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.520
and trigger targeted marketing activities to&nbsp;
remediate; a management team can weigh the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.320
risks of investing in their company’s expansion&nbsp;
based on cash flow analysis and forecasting.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.680
Prescriptive analytics
The purpose of prescriptive analytics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.640
is to literally prescribe what action to take to&nbsp;
eliminate a future problem or take full advantage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.000
of a promising trend. This state-of-the-art&nbsp;
type of data analytics requires not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.040
historical data, but also external information&nbsp;
due to the nature of statistical algorithms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.840
Besides, prescriptive analytics uses sophisticated&nbsp;
tools and technologies, like machine learning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.160
business rules and algorithms, which makes&nbsp;
it sophisticated to implement and manage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.040
That is why, before deciding to&nbsp;
adopt prescriptive analytics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.880
a company should compare required&nbsp;
efforts vs. an expected added value.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.800
What types of data analytics do companies choose?

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:32.320
For the Global Data and Analytics Survey: Big&nbsp;
Decisions, PwC asked more than 2,000 executives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:37.920
to choose a category that describes their&nbsp;
company’s decision-making process best. Further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:43.920
C-suite was questioned with what type of analytics&nbsp;
they rely on most. The results were the following:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.200
descriptive analytics dominates (58%) in the&nbsp;
“Rarely data-driven decision-making” category;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.840
diagnostic analytics tops the list (34%)&nbsp;
in the “Somewhat data-driven” category,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.560
while it is closely followed by descriptive&nbsp;
(29%) and prescriptive (28%) analytics;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.080
predictive analytics (36%) leads in&nbsp;
the “Highly data-driven” category.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.560
This survey proves that at different&nbsp;
stages of a company’s development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.600
there appears a need for one&nbsp;
or the other type of analytics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.960
In fact, the companies that strive for&nbsp;
informed decision-making, find descriptive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.400
analytics insufficient, and add up diagnostics&nbsp;
analytics or even go as far as predictive one.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.440
The same survey reveals another trend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.680
Executives want decision-making to be faster&nbsp;
and more sophisticated. This means that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.840
more businesses will strive to gradually&nbsp;
enlarge the share of predictive analytics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:49.680
Another survey of business intelligence trends&nbsp;
for 2017 carried by BARC proves this hypothesis:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.840
2,800 executives confirmed the growing importance&nbsp;
of predictive analytics and data mining.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.840
In summary, with various types of analytics,&nbsp;
companies are free to choose how deep they need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:12.080
to dive in data analysis to satisfy their business&nbsp;
needs best. While descriptive and diagnostic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.840
analytics offers a reactive approach, predictive&nbsp;
and prescriptive analytics makes users proactive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.080
Meanwhile, current trends show that&nbsp;
more and more companies come to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:33.600
the situation when they need advanced&nbsp;
data analysis, and choose to adopt it.

